  "observed": [
    "A one-person pre-call selection invokes startCall and produces standard one-to-one signaling even when the selector was opened from a group chat.",
    "A multi-person pre-call selection invokes startGroupCall and produces one initial group offer containing all selected users and devices.",
    "A startGroupCall may carry a real group JID or an empty group JID; ad-hoc group calls are not bound to a chat.",
    "Adding people to an active call uses one inviteToCall invocation and one offer per added user.",
    "Group-call identity and routing cannot be inferred from the UI origin or from GroupJID presence alone.",
    "Only connected devices receive PIDs and become active media/keying participants."
